-- statement:
--   This is a finite fragment of an exact linear-real covering proof for the source's annotated word boxes. Its context records coordinate restrictions in addition to the initial density or potential inequalities. At an empty leaf, a nonnegative integer combination gives a contradiction. At a word leaf, such combinations establish every box-coordinate bound.
--
--   $$s\,a_{\mathrm{target}}\le\sum_j\lambda_j a_j,\qquad s>0,\quad\lambda_j\ge0.$$
--
--   Strictness is recorded explicitly. Coordinate cuts connect the leaves, and separate exact checks validate this proof data. Referenced fragments are ordinary child proof fragments, allowing finite verification to be partitioned without changing the real domain.
-- source:
--   Fujiwara, Gutowski, Ouchi and Wolff, STOC 2027 submission #885, Section 3 equation (2) and its proof, printed p. 8 (PDF p. 9), Section 4 Table 1 and verification, printed pp. 9–11 (PDF pp. 10–12), https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/885.pdf. Certificate family P9; explicit linear-combination proof of a fragment of query (4) or (5).

